<p style="margin:4px 0;font-size:12px;opacity:0.8">CVE Security Advisory — Critical Severity</p>
</div>
<div style="padding:24px">

<p>A critical vulnerability has been identified in the <b>tower-lsp</b> Rust crate (versions 0.20.0 through 0.20.1) that affects your repository <b>vigilyx/gateway</b>.</p>

<h3>一、Vulnerability Details</h3>
<table cellpadding=6 style="border-collapse:collapse;border:1px solid #ccc;width:100%">
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5;width:180px">CVE ID</td><td><b>CVE-2026-45912</b></td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">CVSS v3.1 Score</td><td style="color:#e00"><b>9.8 CRITICAL</b> (AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Affected Component</td><td>tower-lsp (LSP server framework for Rust)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Affected Versions</td><td>0.20.0 – 0.20.1</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Fixed Version</td><td style="color:#0a0"><b>0.20.2</b> (released 2026-10-25)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">CWE</td><td>CWE-94 (Improper Control of Code Generation)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Discovery</td><td>2026-10-22 by Google Project Zero</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Exploit Status</td><td style="color:#e00"><b>Known exploited in the wild</b></td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Your Exposure</td><td style="color:#e00"><b>vigilyx/gateway uses tower-lsp 0.20.1</b></td></tr>
</table>

<h3>二、Technical Description</h3>
<p>The vulnerability exists in tower-lsp's handling of the LSP <code>initialize</code> request. A malicious language server can embed a specially crafted <code>rootUri</code> field containing a <b>Rust format string injection</b>. When tower-lsp processes this URI, it passes unsanitized input to a <code>format!()</code> macro, allowing the attacker to:</p>
<ul>
<li>Read arbitrary stack memory (format string <code>{}</code> leaks)</li>
<li>Write to arbitrary memory locations (format string <code>{n$}</code>)</li>
<li>Execute arbitrary code via control-flow hijack</li>
</ul>

<h3>三、Impact on Your Repository</h3>
<p>NVD's automated dependency scanning has identified the following in <b>vigilyx/gateway</b>:</p>
<table cellpadding=5 style="border-collapse:collapse;border:1px solid #ccc;width:100%">
<tr style="background:#f0f0f0"><th>Dependency</th><th>Current Version</th><th>Vulnerable?</th></tr>
<tr><td>tower-lsp</td><td>0.20.1</td><td style="color:#e00"><b>YES</b></td></tr>
<tr><td>tokio</td><td>1.40.2</td><td>No</td></tr>
<tr><td>serde</td><td>1.0.210</td><td>No</td></tr>
</table>
<p><b>Your gateway's LSP handler is directly exploitable</b> if it accepts connections from untrusted language servers.</p>

